from under the sill of the window that this plan would never do at all,

185
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:39,439
especially as another current from the rickety door met the one from the

186
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:43,357
window, and both together formed a series of small whirlwinds in the

187
00:14:43,358 --> 00:14:48,158
immediate vicinity of the spot where I had thought to spend the night. The

188
00:14:48,159 --> 00:14:53,038
devil fetched that harpineer, thought I, but stop. Couldn't I steal a march on

189
00:14:53,039 --> 00:14:57,919
him, bolt his door inside, and jump into his bed, not to be wakened by the most

190
00:14:57,920 --> 00:15:02,558
violent knockings? It seemed no bad idea, but upon second thoughts, I

191
00:15:02,559 --> 00:15:06,638
dismissed it. For who could tell but what the next morning, so soon as I

192
00:15:06,639 --> 00:15:10,158
popped out of the room, the harpineer might be standing in the entry, all

193
00:15:10,159 --> 00:15:15,279
ready to knock me down. Still looking around me again and seeing no possible

194
00:15:15,280 --> 00:15:19,919
chance of spending a sufferable night unless in some other person's bed, I

195
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:24,638
began to think that after all I might be cherishing unwarrantable prejudices

196
00:15:24,639 --> 00:15:30,078
against this unknown harpooner. Thinks I I'll wait a while. He must be dropping

197
00:15:30,079 --> 00:15:34,479
in before long. I'll have a good look at him then, and perhaps we may become

198
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:38,558
jolly good bedfellows after all. There's no telling.

199
00:15:38,559 --> 00:15:42,797
But though the other borders kept coming in by ones, twos, and threes, and going

200
00:15:42,798 --> 00:15:46,638
to bed, yet no sign of my harpooner.

201
00:15:46,639 --> 00:15:52,158
Landlord, said I, what sort of chap is he? Does he always keep such late hours?

202
00:15:52,159 --> 00:15:54,959
It was now hard upon 12:00.

203
00:15:54,960 --> 00:15:59,118
The landlord chuckled again with his lean chuckle, and seemed to be mightily

204
00:15:59,119 --> 00:16:02,797
tickled at something beyond my comprehension.

205
00:16:02,798 --> 00:16:07,439
No, he answered. Generally, he's an early bird. Early to bed and early to

206
00:16:07,440 --> 00:16:12,558
rise. Yes, he's the bird what catches the worm. But tonight he went out to

207
00:16:12,559 --> 00:16:17,198
peddling, you see, and I don't see what on earth keeps him so late, unless maybe

208
00:16:17,199 --> 00:16:23,598
he can't sell his head. Can't sell his head? What sort of a bamboozlingly story

209
00:16:23,599 --> 00:16:28,399
is this you're telling me? Getting into a towering rage. Do you pretend to say,

210
00:16:28,400 --> 00:16:32,479
landlord, that this harpooner is actually engaged this blessed Saturday

211
00:16:32,480 --> 00:16:37,759
night, or rather Sunday morning, in pedalling his head around town?

212
00:16:37,760 --> 00:16:42,559
That's precisely it, said the landlord, and I told him he couldn't sell it here.

213
00:16:42,560 --> 00:16:45,118
The markets overstocked.

214
00:16:45,119 --> 00:16:48,879
With what, shouted I heads, to be sure.

215
00:16:48,880 --> 00:16:52,237
Ain't there too many heads in the world?

216
00:16:52,238 --> 00:16:56,959
I tell you what it is, landlord, I said quite calmly. You'd better stop spinning

217
00:16:56,960 --> 00:17:00,157
that yarn to me. I am not green.

218
00:17:00,158 --> 00:17:04,797
Maybe not, taking a stick out and whittling a toothpick. But I rather

219
00:17:04,798 --> 00:17:09,999
guess you'll be done brown if that air harper hears you a slander in his head.

220
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:14,078
I'll break it for him, said I, now flying into a passion against this

221
00:17:14,079 --> 00:17:17,118
unaccountable furago of the landlords.

222
00:17:17,119 --> 00:17:24,157
It's broke already, said he. Broke, said I. Broke, do you mean? certain, and

223
00:17:24,158 --> 00:17:27,999
that's the very reason he can't sell it, I guess.

224
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:33,999
Landlord, said I, going up to him as cool as Mount Heekla in a snowstorm.

225
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:38,879
Landlord, stop whittling. You and I must understand one another, and that too

226
00:17:38,880 --> 00:17:43,678
without delay. I come to your house and want a bed. You tell me you can only

227
00:17:43,679 --> 00:17:48,318
give me half of one, that the other half belongs to a certain harpooner. And

228
00:17:48,319 --> 00:17:52,639
about this harpooner whom I have not yet seen, you persist in telling me the most

229
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:57,197
mystifying and exasperating stories, tending to beget in me an uncomfortable

230
00:17:57,198 --> 00:18:01,678
feeling towards the man whom you designed for my bedfellow, a sort of

231
00:18:01,679 --> 00:18:05,278
connection, landlord, which is an intimate and confidential one in the

232
00:18:05,279 --> 00:18:10,318
highest degree. I now demand of you to speak out and tell me who and what this

233
00:18:10,319 --> 00:18:14,879
harpooner is, and whether I shall be in all respects safe to spend the night

234
00:18:14,880 --> 00:18:19,438
with him. And in the first place you will be so good as to unsay that story

235
00:18:19,439 --> 00:18:23,678
about selling his head, which if true, I take to be good evidence that this

236
00:18:23,679 --> 00:18:29,358
harpooner is stark mad, and I have no idea of sleeping with a madman. And you,

237
00:18:29,359 --> 00:18:36,318
sir, you I mean, landlord, you sir, by trying to induce me to do so knowingly,

238
00:18:36,319 --> 00:18:42,318
would thereby render yourself liable to a criminal prosecution?

239
00:18:42,319 --> 00:18:47,197
Well, said the landlord, fetching a long breath. That's a pretty long sermon for

240
00:18:47,198 --> 00:18:52,318
a chap that rips a little now and then, "But be easy, be easy. This here

241
00:18:52,319 --> 00:18:56,879
harpooner I've been telling you of, has just arrived from the South Seas, where

242
00:18:56,880 --> 00:19:01,999
he bought up a lot of bomb New Zealand heads, great curios, you know, and he

243
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,237
sold all of them but one. And that one he's trying to sell tonight cuz

244
00:19:06,238 --> 00:19:10,639
tomorrow's Sunday and it would not do to be selling human heads about the streets

245
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:15,839
when folks is going to churches. He wanted to last Sunday, but I stopped him

246
00:19:15,840 --> 00:19:20,398
just as he was going out the door with four heads strung on a string for all

247
00:19:20,399 --> 00:19:23,839
the earth like a string of enions.

248
00:19:23,840 --> 00:19:27,599
This account cleared up the otherwise unaccountable mystery and showed that

249
00:19:27,600 --> 00:19:32,318
the landlord, after all, had no idea of fooling me. But at the same time, what

250
00:19:32,319 --> 00:19:36,237
could I think of a harpooner who stayed out of a Saturday night clean into the

251
00:19:36,238 --> 00:19:42,478
holy Sabbath, engaged in such a cannibal business as selling the heads of dead idoltors?

252
00:19:42,479 --> 00:19:49,197
Depend upon it, landlord, that harpooner is a dangerous man. He pays regular, was

253
00:19:49,198 --> 00:19:53,919
the rejoinder. But come, it's getting dreadful late. You'd better be turning

254
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:58,718
flukes. It's a nice bed. S and me slept in that air bed the night we was

255
00:19:58,719 --> 00:20:03,197
spliced. There's plenty of room for two to kick about in that bed. It's an

256
00:20:03,198 --> 00:20:08,157
almighty big bed. That why, before we give it up, S used to put our Sam and

257
00:20:08,158 --> 00:20:12,639
little Johnny in the foot of it. But I got a dreaming and sprawling about one

258
00:20:12,640 --> 00:20:17,038
night, and somehow Sam got pitched on the floor and came near breaking his

259
00:20:17,039 --> 00:20:21,919
arm. After that, Sal said it wouldn't do. Come along here. I'll give you a

260
00:20:21,920 --> 00:20:26,718
glimp in a jify. And so, saying, he lighted a candle and held it towards me,

261
00:20:26,719 --> 00:20:31,519
offering to lead the way. But I stood irresolute. When looking at a clock in

262
00:20:31,520 --> 00:20:35,999
the corner, he exclaimed, "I vomit Sunday. You won't see that hopping

263
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,078
tonight. He's come to anchor somewhere.

264
00:20:38,079 --> 00:20:43,678
Come along then. Do come, won't you come?" I considered the matter a moment,

265
00:20:43,679 --> 00:20:49,038
and then upstairs we went. And I was ushered into a small room, cold as a

266
00:20:49,039 --> 00:20:53,678
clam, and furnished, sure enough, with a prodigious bed, almost big enough

267
00:20:53,679 --> 00:20:59,038
indeed, for any four harpooners to sleep a breast. There, said the landlord,

268
00:20:59,039 --> 00:21:03,438
placing the candle on their crazy old sea chest that did double duty as a wash

269
00:21:03,439 --> 00:21:07,839
stand and center table. There, make yourself comfortable now, and good night

270
00:21:07,840 --> 00:21:13,599
to you. I turned round from eyeing the bed, but he had disappeared.

271
00:21:13,600 --> 00:21:17,999
Folding back the counterpane, I stood over the bed. Though none of the most

272
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:22,799
elegant, it yet stood the scrutiny tolerable well. I then glanced around

273
00:21:22,800 --> 00:21:26,398
the room, and besides the bedstead and center table, could see no other

274
00:21:26,399 --> 00:21:30,718
furniture belonging to the place, but a rude shelf, the four walls, and a

275
00:21:30,719 --> 00:21:35,919
papered fireboard representing a man striking a whale. Of things not properly

276
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:39,839
belonging to the room, there was a hammock lashed up and thrown upon the

277
00:21:39,840 --> 00:21:44,237
floor in one corner, also a large seaman's bag containing the harpooner's

278
00:21:44,238 --> 00:21:49,519
wardrobe, no doubt in lie of a land trunk. Likewise, there was a parcel of

279
00:21:49,520 --> 00:21:54,718
outlandish bone fish hooks on the shelf over the fireplace and a tall harpoon

280
00:21:54,719 --> 00:22:00,559
standing at the head of the bed. But what is this on the chest? I took it up

281
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:04,959
and held it close to the light and felt it and smelt it and tried every way

282
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:09,839
possible to arrive at some satisfactory conclusion concerning it. I can compare

283
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:13,839
it to nothing but a large doormat ornamented at the edges with little

284
00:22:13,840 --> 00:22:18,718
tinkling tags, something like the stained porcupine quills round an Indian

285
00:22:18,719 --> 00:22:23,197
moccasin. There was a hole or slit in the middle of this mat as you see the

286
00:22:23,198 --> 00:22:27,678
same in South American ponchos. But could it be possible that any sober

287
00:22:27,679 --> 00:22:32,078
harpooner could get into a doormat and parade the streets of any Christian town

288
00:22:32,079 --> 00:22:35,197
in that sort of guys? I put it on to try

289
00:22:35,198 --> 00:22:39,038
it, and it weighed me down like a hamper, being uncommonly shaggy and

290
00:22:39,039 --> 00:22:43,278
thick, and I thought a little damp, as though this mysterious harpooner had

291
00:22:43,279 --> 00:22:45,919
been wearing it of a rainy day. I went

292
00:22:45,920 --> 00:22:47,919
up to it in a bit of glass stuck against

293
00:22:47,920 --> 00:22:50,237
the wall, and I never saw such a sight

294
00:22:50,238 --> 00:22:52,799
in my life. I tore myself out of it in

295
00:22:52,800 --> 00:22:54,718
such a hurry that I gave myself a kink

296
00:22:54,719 --> 00:22:59,278
in the neck. I sat down on the side of the bed, and commenced thinking about

297
00:22:59,279 --> 00:23:04,718
this headpedling harpooner in his doormat. After thinking some time on the

298
00:23:04,719 --> 00:23:08,799
bedside, I got up and took off my monkey jacket, and then stood in the middle of

299
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:13,118
the room, thinking. Then I took off my coat and thought a little more in my

300
00:23:13,119 --> 00:23:18,157
shirt sleeves. But beginning to feel very cold now, half undressed as I was,

301
00:23:18,158 --> 00:23:21,999
and remembering what the landlord said about the harpooners not coming home at

302
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:27,038
all that night, it being so very late, I made no more ado, but jumped out of my

303
00:23:27,039 --> 00:23:31,759
pantaloons and boots, and then, blowing out the light, tumbled into bed, and

304
00:23:31,760 --> 00:23:35,519
commended myself to the care of heaven.

305
00:23:35,520 --> 00:23:40,078
Whether that mattress was stuffed with corn cobs or broken crockery there is no

306
00:23:40,079 --> 00:23:45,118
telling but I rolled about a good deal and could not sleep for a long time. At

307
00:23:45,119 --> 00:23:49,678
last I slid off into a light doze and had pretty nearly made a good offing

308
00:23:49,679 --> 00:23:54,237
towards the land of nod when I heard a heavy footfall in the passage and saw a

309
00:23:54,238 --> 00:23:59,358
glimmer of light come into the room from under the door. Lord save me thinks I

310
00:23:59,359 --> 00:24:03,038
that must be the harpineer the infernal headpedler.

311
00:24:03,039 --> 00:24:07,919
But I lay perfectly still and resolved not to say a word till spoken to.

312
00:24:07,920 --> 00:24:12,559
Holding a light in one hand and that identical New Zealand head in the other,

313
00:24:12,560 --> 00:24:16,398
the stranger entered the room, and without looking towards the bed, placed

314
00:24:16,399 --> 00:24:20,799
his candle a good way off from me on the floor in one corner, and then began

315
00:24:20,800 --> 00:24:25,599
working away at the knotted cords of the large bag I before spoke of as being in

316
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:30,398
the room. I was all eagerness to see his face, but he kept it averted for some

317
00:24:30,399 --> 00:24:35,118
time while employed in unlacing the bag's mouth. This accomplished, however,

318
00:24:35,119 --> 00:24:41,358
he turned round when, good heavens, what a sight, such a face. It was of a dark

319
00:24:41,359 --> 00:24:46,078
purplish yellow color here and there, stuck over with large blackishl looking

320
00:24:46,079 --> 00:24:48,799
squares. Yes, it's just as I thought.

321
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:53,678
He's a terrible bed fellow. He's been in a fight, got dreadfully cut, and here he

322
00:24:53,679 --> 00:24:58,237
is, just from the surgeon. But at that moment he chanced to turn his face so

323
00:24:58,238 --> 00:25:02,318
towards the light that I plainly saw they could not be sticking plasters at

324
00:25:02,319 --> 00:25:05,438
all, those black squares on his cheeks.

325
00:25:05,439 --> 00:25:07,919
They were stains of some sort or other.

326
00:25:07,920 --> 00:25:12,639
At first I knew not what to make of this, but soon an inkling of the truth

327
00:25:12,640 --> 00:25:17,999
occurred to me. I remembered a story of a white man, a whaleman too, who falling

328
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:22,639
among the cannibals had been tattooed by them. I concluded that this harpooner,

329
00:25:22,640 --> 00:25:27,197
in the course of his distant voyages, must have met with a similar adventure.

330
00:25:27,198 --> 00:25:29,438
And what is it, thought I, after all?

331
00:25:29,439 --> 00:25:34,478
It's only his outside. A man can be honest in any sort of skin. But then,

332
00:25:34,479 --> 00:25:37,197
what to make of his unearly complexion?

333
00:25:37,198 --> 00:25:41,197
That part of it, I mean, lying round about and completely independent of the

334
00:25:41,198 --> 00:25:45,519
squares of tattooing. To be sure, it might be nothing but a good coat of

335
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:50,237
tropical tanning, but I never heard of a hot sun tanning a white man into a

336
00:25:50,238 --> 00:25:54,639
purplish yellow one. However, I had never been in the South Seas, and

337
00:25:54,640 --> 00:25:59,278
perhaps the sun there produced these extraordinary effects upon the skin.

338
00:25:59,279 --> 00:26:02,559
Now, while all these ideas were passing through me like lightning, this

339
00:26:02,560 --> 00:26:07,438
harpooner never noticed me at all. But after some difficulty having opened his

340
00:26:07,439 --> 00:26:11,278
bag, he commenced fumbling in it, and presently pulled out a sort of a

341
00:26:11,279 --> 00:26:16,559
tomahawk and a seal skin wallet with the hair on. Putting these on the old chest

342
00:26:16,560 --> 00:26:20,879
in the middle of the room, he then took the New Zealand head, a ghastly thing

343
00:26:20,880 --> 00:26:25,759
enough, and crammed it down into the bag. He now took off his hat, a new

344
00:26:25,760 --> 00:26:30,959
beaver hat. When I came nigh singing out with fresh surprise, there was no hair

345
00:26:30,960 --> 00:26:35,839
on his head, none to speak of, at least, nothing but a small scalp knot twisted

346
00:26:35,840 --> 00:26:40,398
upon his forehead. His bald purplish head now looked for all the world like a

347
00:26:40,399 --> 00:26:45,197
mild skull. Had not the stranger stood between me and the door, I would have

348
00:26:45,198 --> 00:26:50,078
bolted out of it quicker than I ever bolted a dinner. Even as it was, I

349
00:26:50,079 --> 00:26:53,999
thought something of slipping out the window, but it was the second floor

350
00:26:54,000 --> 00:26:58,639
back. I am no coward, but what to make of this headpedling purple rascal

351
00:26:58,640 --> 00:27:01,438
altogether past my comprehension.

352
00:27:01,439 --> 00:27:05,759
Ignorance is the parent of fear, and being completely non-plust and

353
00:27:05,760 --> 00:27:09,278
confounded about the stranger, I confessed I was now as much afraid of

354
00:27:09,279 --> 00:27:13,678
him, as if it was the devil himself who had thus broken into my room in the dead

355
00:27:13,679 --> 00:27:18,237
of night. In fact, I was so afraid of him that I was not game enough just then

356
00:27:18,238 --> 00:27:25,197
to address him, and demand a satisfactory answer concerning what seemed inexplicable in him.

357
00:27:25,198 --> 00:27:29,438
Meanwhile, he continued the business of undressing, and at last showed his chest

358
00:27:29,439 --> 00:27:33,919
and arms. As I live, these covered parts of him were checkered with the same

359
00:27:33,920 --> 00:27:39,358
squares as his face. His back, too, was all over the same dark squares. He

360
00:27:39,359 --> 00:27:43,438
seemed to have been in a 30 years war, and just escaped from it with a sticking

361
00:27:43,439 --> 00:27:49,118
plaster shirt. Still more, his very legs were marked as if a parcel of dark green

362
00:27:49,119 --> 00:27:53,839
frogs were running up the trunks of young palms. It was now quite plain that

363
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:57,599
he must be some abominable savage or other shipped aboard of a whaleman in

364
00:27:57,600 --> 00:28:02,398
the South Seas and so landed in this Christian country. I quake to think of

365
00:28:02,399 --> 00:28:07,678
it, a peddler of heads, too. Perhaps the heads of his own brothers. He might take

366
00:28:07,679 --> 00:28:11,839
a fancy to mind. Heavens, look at that tomahawk.

367
00:28:11,840 --> 00:28:15,678
But there was no time for shuddering, for now the savage went about something

368
00:28:15,679 --> 00:28:20,078
that completely fascinated my attention and convinced me that he must indeed be

369
00:28:20,079 --> 00:28:25,278
a heathen. Going to his heavy grego or raffle or dreadnot which he had

370
00:28:25,279 --> 00:28:29,599
previously hung on a chair, he fumbled in the pockets and produced at length a

371
00:28:29,600 --> 00:28:33,999
curious little deformed image with a hunch on its back and exactly the color

372
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:39,519
of a 3 days old Congo baby. remembering the imbalmed head at first I almost

373
00:28:39,520 --> 00:28:43,519
thought that this black mannequin was a real baby preserved in some similar

374
00:28:43,520 --> 00:28:47,839
manner. But seeing that it was not at all limber and that it glistened a good

375
00:28:47,840 --> 00:28:52,237
deal like polished ebony, I concluded that it must be nothing but a wooden

376
00:28:52,238 --> 00:28:57,038
idol, which indeed it proved to be. For now the savage goes up to the empty

377
00:28:57,039 --> 00:29:01,358
fireplace and removing the papered fireboard sets up this little

378
00:29:01,359 --> 00:29:06,478
hunchbacked image like a tenpin between the and irons. The chimney jams and all

379
00:29:06,479 --> 00:29:10,639
the bricks inside were very sy that I thought this fireplace made a very

380
00:29:10,640 --> 00:29:16,398
appropriate little shrine or chapel for his Congo idol. I now screwed my eyes

381
00:29:16,399 --> 00:29:20,639
hard toward the half-hidden image feeling but ill at ease meantime to see

382
00:29:20,640 --> 00:29:25,278
what was next to follow. First he takes about a double handful of shavings out

383
00:29:25,279 --> 00:29:30,478
of his grego pocket and places them carefully before the idol. Then laying a

384
00:29:30,479 --> 00:29:35,038
bit of ship biscuit on top and applying the flame from the lamp, he kindled the

385
00:29:35,039 --> 00:29:37,759
shavings into a sacrificial blaze.

386
00:29:37,760 --> 00:29:41,839
Presently, after many hasty snatches into the fire, and still hastier

387
00:29:41,840 --> 00:29:46,879
withdraws of his fingers, whereby he seemed to be scorching them badly, he at

388
00:29:46,880 --> 00:29:50,799
last succeeded in drawing out the biscuit. Then blowing off the heat and

389
00:29:50,800 --> 00:29:55,358
ashes a little, he made a polite offer of it to the little negro, but the

390
00:29:55,359 --> 00:30:00,398
little devil did not seem to fancy such dry sort of fair at all. He never moved

391
00:30:00,399 --> 00:30:05,999
his lips. All these strange antics were accompanied by still stranger guttural

392
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:10,718
noises from the devote who seemed to be praying in a sing song, or else singing

393
00:30:10,719 --> 00:30:15,118
some pagan somdy or other, during which his face twitched about in the most

394
00:30:15,119 --> 00:30:20,318
unnatural manner. At last extinguishing the fire, he took his idol up very

395
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:25,278
unceremoniously and bagged it again in his grego pocket as carelessly as if he

396
00:30:25,279 --> 00:30:28,718
were a sportsman bagging a dead woodcock.

397
00:30:28,719 --> 00:30:33,118
All these queer proceedings increased my uncomfortableness, and seeing him now

398
00:30:33,119 --> 00:30:37,519
exhibiting strong symptoms of concluding his business operations and jumping into

399
00:30:37,520 --> 00:30:41,678
bed with me, I thought it was high time, now or never, before the light was put

400
00:30:41,679 --> 00:30:46,799
out, to break the spell in which I had so long been bound. But the interval I

401
00:30:46,800 --> 00:30:51,519
spent in deliberating what to say was a fatal one. Taking his tomahawk from the

402
00:30:51,520 --> 00:30:55,358
table, he examined the head of it for an instant, and then holding it to the

403
00:30:55,359 --> 00:30:59,519
light with his mouth at the handle, he puffed out great clouds of tobacco

404
00:30:59,520 --> 00:31:04,237
smoke. The next moment the light was extinguished, and this wild cannibal

405
00:31:04,238 --> 00:31:08,879
tomahawk between his teeth, sprang into bed with me. I sang out. I could not

406
00:31:08,880 --> 00:31:14,078
help it now, and giving a sudden grunt of astonishment, he began feeling me.

407
00:31:14,079 --> 00:31:17,839
Stammering out something, I knew not what, I rolled away from him against the

408
00:31:17,840 --> 00:31:22,559
wall, and then conjured him, whoever or whatever he might be, to keep quiet, and

409
00:31:22,560 --> 00:31:24,799
let me get up and light the lamp again.

410
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:29,519
But his guttural responses satisfied me at once that he but ill comprehended my

411
00:31:29,520 --> 00:31:36,078
meaning. "Who devil you?" he said at last. "You no speak yey, damn me, I kill

412
00:31:36,079 --> 00:31:42,237
ye." And so saying, the lighted tomahawk began flourishing about me in the dark.

413
00:31:42,238 --> 00:31:48,638
Landlord, for God's sake, Peter Coffin, shouted I. Landlord, watch. Coffin,

414
00:31:48,639 --> 00:31:55,278
angel, save me. Speaky. Telly me who he be, or damn me, I kill you. Again,

415
00:31:55,279 --> 00:31:59,358
growled the cannibal, while his horrid flourishings of the tomahawk scattered

416
00:31:59,359 --> 00:32:03,999
the hot tobacco ashes about me, till I thought my linen would get on fire. But

417
00:32:04,000 --> 00:32:07,519
thank heaven, at that moment the landlord came into the room, light in

418
00:32:07,520 --> 00:32:11,599
hand, and leaping from the bed, I ran up to him.

419
00:32:11,600 --> 00:32:16,879
Don't be afraid now, said he, grinning again. Quiqu here wouldn't harm a hair

420
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:21,599
of your head. Stop your grinning, shouted I. And why didn't you tell me

421
00:32:21,600 --> 00:32:26,478
that that infernal harpooner was a cannibal? I thought you'd know it.

422
00:32:26,479 --> 00:32:31,278
Didn't I tell you he was a peddling heads around town? But turn flukes again

423
00:32:31,279 --> 00:32:37,919
and go to sleep. Quig, look here. You sabby me, I sabby you. This man sleepy

424
00:32:37,920 --> 00:32:46,799
you. You sabi me sabi plenty grunted Quequ puffing away at his pipe and sitting up in bed.

425
00:32:46,800 --> 00:32:51,678
You get in, he added, motioning to me with his tomahawk and throwing the

426
00:32:51,679 --> 00:32:56,799
clothes to one side. He really did this in not only a civil but really a kind

427
00:32:56,800 --> 00:33:01,919
and charitable way. I stood looking at him a moment. For all his tattooings he

428
00:33:01,920 --> 00:33:06,318
was on the whole a clean, cumblyl looking cannibal. What's all this fuss I

429
00:33:06,319 --> 00:33:10,318
have been making about? thought I to myself. The man's a human being just as

430
00:33:10,319 --> 00:33:12,959
I am. He has as much reason to fear me

431
00:33:12,960 --> 00:33:19,678
as I have to be afraid of him. Better sleep with a sober cannibal than a drunken Christian.

432
00:33:19,679 --> 00:33:24,638
Landlord, said I, tell him to stash his tomahawk there, or pipe, or whatever you

433
00:33:24,639 --> 00:33:29,438
call it. Tell him to stop smoking, in short, and I will turn in with him. But

434
00:33:29,439 --> 00:33:34,398
I don't fancy having a man smoking in bed with me. It's dangerous. Besides, I

435
00:33:34,399 --> 00:33:39,519
ain't insured. This being told to Quiquake, he at once complied, and again

436
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:44,237
politely motioned me to get into bed, rolling over to one side as much to say,

437
00:33:44,238 --> 00:33:47,118
I won't touch a leg of you.

438
00:33:47,119 --> 00:33:56,679
Good night, landlord, said I. You may go. I turned in and never slept better in my life.
